      "readme_excerpt": "YOLO3D is inspired by Mousavian et al. in their paper **3D Bounding Box Estimation Using Deep Learning and Geometry**. YOLO3D uses a different approach, we use 2d gt label result as the input of first stage detector, then use the 2d result as input to regressor model. git clone git@github.com:ApolloAuto/apollo-model-yolo3d.git cd apollo-model-yolo3d conda create -n apollo_yolo3d python=3.8 numpy conda activate apollo_yolo3d pip install -r requirements.txt here we use KITTI data to train. You can download KITTI dataset from official website. After that, extract dataset to `data/KITTI`. ln -s /your/KITTI/path data/KITTI ├── data │ └── KITTI │ ├── calib │ ├──",
